    <main>
        <h1>LeetCode 3364: Minimum Positive Sum Subarray (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given an integer array nums and two integers l and r. Your task is to find the
                minimum sum of a subarray whose size is between l and r (inclusive) and whose sum is greater
                than 0. Return the minimum sum of such a subarray. If no such subarray exists, return -1. A
                subarray is a contiguous non-empty sequence of elements within an array.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: nums = [3,-2,1,4], l = 2, r = 3<br>
                Output: 1<br>
                Explanation: The subarrays of length between l = 2 and r = 3 where the sum is greater than 0
                are [3,-2] with sum 1, [1,4] with sum 5, [3,-2,1] with sum 2, and [-2,1,4] with sum 3. Out
                of these, the subarray [3,-2] has the minimum positive sum of 1.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int minimumSumSubarray(vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; nums, int l, int r) {
        int n = nums.size(), mn = INT_MAX;

        for (int i = 0; i &lt; n; i++) {
            int sum = 0;

            for (int j = i; j &lt; n; j++) {
                sum += nums[j];
                int len = j - i + 1;

                if (len &gt;= l &amp;&amp; len &lt;= r &amp;&amp; sum &gt; 0)
                    mn = min(mn, sum);
            }
        }

        return mn == INT_MAX ? -1 : mn;
    }
};</code></pre>
